<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (Phishing is a cyberattack technique in which attackers create fraudulent websites that imitate trusted organizations to steal confidential information from users. With the increasing number of online transactions and digital services, phishing attacks have become more frequent and sophisticated.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 65 0 R
/E (Traditional phishing detection methods depend on manually updated blacklists and predefined rules, making them ineffective against newly generated phishing websites. Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning provide an efficient alternative by learning patterns from datasets and identifying malicious URLs based on extracted features.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
